{% doc %}
  The collector card, at the top of the media column on the Tee of the Week.

  @param {string} card_url - The rendered card image. The caller decides whether
    to show it; this snippet does not re-test, because the block needs the same
    answer to collapse the gallery and Liquid cannot read a variable back out of
    a render.
  @param {object} product - The product, for the alt text.

  WHY IT IS NOT THE PRODUCT IMAGE. The obvious version is to add the rendered
  card to the product's media so it simply becomes the first photo. That would
  also push it into the Google and Meta feeds — and Merchant Center prohibits
  promotional overlays on product images. The card has "15% OFF ALL WEEK" and a
  struck price burned into it, so that route would inject a policy violation
  into the feed of an account already suspended once for misrepresentation.

  So it renders here, on the page, and never enters the catalogue.

  The URL arrives from `enrich.tee_card_url`, a storefront-readable product
  metafield, rather than the tee_week metaobject — that one is
  `storefront: NONE`, and opening it up would expose the queue, including which
  tees are coming in later weeks.
{% enddoc %}

{%- if card_url != blank -%}
  <figure class="aj-teecard">
    <img
      src="{{ card_url }}"
      alt="Tee of the Week collector card for {{ product.title | escape }}"
      width="1080"
      height="1350"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      class="aj-teecard__img"
    >
  </figure>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    IT IS A CARD, SO IT SHOULD BE CARD-SIZED. At full column width the thing
    read as a billboard — on desktop it filled half the page, on a phone it took
    the whole screen before anyone reached the price. The object it is imitating
    is something you hold in one hand, and the proportions have to say that or
    the whole conceit collapses.

    Capped and centred instead. 22rem keeps it comfortably shorter than the
    viewport at 4:5, so the card and the beginning of the buy column are visible
    together.
  */
  .aj-teecard {
    margin: 0 auto var(--padding-md, 1rem);
    max-width: min(100%, 22rem);
  }

  .aj-teecard__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    /* A soft drop rather than a border: the card already draws its own frame,
       and a second edge around it looked like a mistake. */
    filter: drop-shadow(0 6px 18px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.18));
  }

  /* ---- the disclosure holding the supplier photographs ------------------- */

  .aj-teecard__more {
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }

  /*
    Same purple uppercase label as the mega menu, the category drill-down and
    the footer contact block. A control that looks like every other label on the
    site does not need explaining.
  */
  .aj-teecard__more-label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding-block: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Safari still paints its own triangle without this. */
  .aj-teecard__more-label::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more-label::after {
    content: "";
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-right: 2px solid currentcolor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentcolor;
    transform: rotate(45deg) translate(-0.1em, -0.1em);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more[open] .aj-teecard__more-label::after {
    transform: rotate(-135deg) translate(-0.15em, -0.15em);
  }

  .aj-teecard__more-label:hover {
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
  }

  /* One label, two states, no JavaScript. */
  .aj-teecard__more [data-when-open] {
    display: none;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more[open] [data-when-open] {
    display: inline;
  }

  .aj-teecard__more[open] [data-when-closed] {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
